<title>BELGIUM: EAT heads Brussels cargo-handing airlines table.</title>
<headline>EAT heads Brussels cargo-handing airlines table.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Air Transport (EAT), a DHL group airline subsidiary, was the top cargo carrier at Brussels airport in 1996, Brussels airport authority figures showed.</p>
<p>The Top 10 cargo-handling airlines at Brussels airport in 1996 in tonnes, with 1995 ranking in brackets, with percentage change on 1995 were:</p>
<p>    1 (1) European Air Transport*    156,569  up    17.2</p>
<p>    2 (2) Sabena			    80,950  down  17.8</p>
<p>    3 (4) DHL Aviation		    41,148  up    53.8</p>
<p>    4 (3) Saudia			    37,447  up     1.6</p>
<p>    5 (5)  Air Hong Kong		  22,486  down   3.7</p>
<p>    6 (6)  Singapore			19,022  down   1.1</p>
<p>    7 (11) Emery*			   14,829  up   226.5</p>
<p>    8 (8)  American Airlines	    10,106  down  31.6</p>
<p>    9 (7)  Gulf Air*			 6,053  down 153.4</p>
<p>    10 (-) Hunting Cargo Airlines*     5,597  n.a</p>
<p>*  operating on behalf of DHL</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
